# Everything here is excluded from the build context — the tarball Docker sends
# to the daemon before the first instruction runs. Two reasons it matters:
#
#   speed — node_modules and .next are hundreds of megabytes; shipping them only
#           to overwrite them with `npm ci` and `next build` wastes the whole
#           transfer on every build.
#
#   safety — .env holds a real database password and a real API key. Without
#            this file, `COPY . .` in the build stage bakes them into an image
#            layer. Deleting the file in a later instruction does NOT remove it:
#            layers are immutable and anyone with the image can read it back.
#            Secrets reach the container from Kubernetes at runtime, never from
#            the image.

node_modules
.next
.git
.gitignore

.env
.env.*

# Local Postgres data and uploaded audio: runtime state, not build input.
public/uploads
postgres-data

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
k8s
README.md

npm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo
